					<li>
						<foundation Class="IdeoFoundation_Deity">
							<def>Deity</def>
							<place>Bagua5</place>
							<deities>
								<li>
									<name>As-Salam</name>
									<type>Creator of All</type>
									<gender>Female</gender>
									<iconPath>UI/Deities/DeityGeneric</iconPath>
									<relatedMeme>TreeConnection</relatedMeme>
								</li>
							</deities>
						</foundation>
						<name>Wild Meadow</name>
						<adjective>Neo-Zahirist</adjective>
						<memberName>Neo-Zahirist</memberName>
						<leaderTitleMale>High Chief</leaderTitleMale>
						<leaderTitleFemale>High Chief</leaderTitleFemale>
						<description>The first settlers that arrived at the junkyard planet Bagua 5 paved over the natural world and killed the animals. &lt;color=#D09B61FF&gt;As-Salam&lt;/color&gt; wiped them out to punish them for their disrespect towards her creations. A junk lord arose and threatened to destroy &lt;color=#D09B61FF&gt;As-Salam&lt;/color&gt; herself using a rust virus. A hero named Casen 'Vulture' Doaenñole tried to assassinate the junk lord. She failed, but &lt;color=#D09B61FF&gt;As-Salam&lt;/color&gt; witnessed Vulture's struggle, and anointed her as the prophet of the Neo-Zahirists. Vulture found the junk lord sleeping in the trader spaceport, and placed an acorn upon the junk lord's chest. With &lt;color=#D09B61FF&gt;As-Salam&lt;/color&gt;'s fierce power it rooted there, growing through his body, taking our revenge on the tree-killer.</description>
						<descriptionTemplate>The first settlers that arrived at the junkyard planet Bagua 5 paved over the natural world and killed the animals. %%Deity0_name%% wiped them out to punish them for their disrespect towards %%deity0_possessive%% creations. A junk lord arose and threatened to destroy %%deity0_name%% %%deity0_objective%%self using a rust virus. A hero named Casen 'Vulture' Doaenñole tried to assassinate the junk lord. She failed, but %%deity0_name%% witnessed Vulture's struggle, and anointed her as the prophet of the %%memberNamePlural%%. Vulture found the junk lord sleeping in the trader spaceport, and placed an acorn upon the junk lord's chest. With %%deity0_name%%'s fierce power it rooted there, growing through his body, taking our revenge on the tree-killer.</descriptionTemplate>
						<culture>Corunan</culture>
						<iconDef>RoundE</iconDef>
						<colorDef>LightBlue</colorDef>
						<primaryFactionColor>RGBA(0.884, 0.697, 0.253, 1.000)</primaryFactionColor>
