						</foundation>
						<name>Ilwaban Cult</name>
						<adjective>victoryist</adjective>
						<memberName>Victorist</memberName>
						<leaderTitleMale>First Chief</leaderTitleMale>
						<leaderTitleFemale>First Chief</leaderTitleFemale>
						<description>The people of the regrown ruin-world Ilwaba worshipped &lt;color=#D09B61FF&gt;Ro'xadabai&lt;/color&gt;. She saw that they were suited for creation, and ordained that these worshippers would rule above all others. A crypto-leader passed a law forbidding Victorists from rising to the ruling classes of Ilwaba. A renowned artifact hunter named Orange Seara brought the Victorists together, and even recruited some of the crypto-soldiers. Orange destroyed the capital of Ilwaba with an archotech mass-inverter, killing the crypto-leader. She took her place as ruler of Ilwaba - and the universe beyond.</description>
						<descriptionTemplate>The people of the regrown ruin-world Ilwaba worshipped %%deity0_name%%. %%Deity0_pronoun%% saw that they were suited for creation, and ordained that these worshippers would rule above all others. A crypto-leader passed a law forbidding %%memberNamePlural%% from rising to the ruling classes of Ilwaba. A renowned artifact hunter named Orange Seara brought the %%memberNamePlural%% together, and even recruited some of the crypto-soldiers. Orange destroyed the capital of Ilwaba with an archotech mass-inverter, killing the crypto-leader. She took her place as ruler of Ilwaba - and the universe beyond.</descriptionTemplate>
						<culture>Corunan</culture>
						<iconDef>AbstractsD</iconDef>
